<<<
tude (as in party &c.), or a straightforward plural without complications about a virtually singular sense (as in wages) or separate items (as in he & she), the verb follows
===
tude (as in *party* &c.), or a straightforward plural without complications about a virtually singular sense (as in *wages*) or separate items (as in *he & she*), the verb follows
>>>

<<<
the rule:—Our only guide were the stars./Its strongest point are ihe diagrams./Hor Germany’s great need are colonies./The plausible suggestions to the contrary so frequently put forward is an endeavour to kill two
===
the rule:—*Our only guide were the stars./Its strongest point are the diagrams./For Germany's great need are colonies./The plausible suggestions to the contrary so frequently put forward is an endeavour to kill two
